From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DjDeveloperr <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:46:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: describe ATC2 and its display
 crossbar

The M4 has four ATCs, but t8132.dtsi describes two. Add the third and
fourth ATC PHYs, their display crossbars, DWC3 controllers and DARTs,
and the second SPMI bus for port controllers (the J604's right-hand
port), all disabled, in a file of their own that boards include.

Addresses and interrupts are from the J604 and J773g ADTs (atc-phy2/3,
usb-drd2/3, dart-usb2/3, atc2/3-dpxbar, nub-spmi-a1).

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>

(backported from commit bdb254df1dd4a236aaaa792494e6cd82f88d7c94)
[j604: ATC2 half only, inline in t8132.dtsi next to ATC3: this tree already describes ATC3, its crossbar, DWC3, DARTs and nub-spmi-a1 there. dwc3_2 and its DARTs are not taken: the J604 ADT has no usb-drd2 or dart-usb2 (they come from the J773g). atcphy2 reg and atc2-dpxbar reg checked against the J604 ADT atc-phy2/atc2-dpxbar; the pipehandler window is usb-drd2's (J773g, upstream value). The atcphy2 alias is left to the boards.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 22983d4ae9..6bfef5fa6b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -1084,6 +1084,43 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * The third ATC. On the J604 it has no USB controller (no usb-drd2
+		 * in its ADT) and is the DisplayPort PHY behind the HDMI port; the
+		 * pipehandler window is usb-drd2's on boards that have one. Leave the
+		 * display crossbar at core + 0x4c000 to its own driver.
+		 */
+		atcphy2: phy@412a90000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-atcphy";
+			reg = <0x4 0x12a90000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x4 0x12a84000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x4 0x13000000 0x0 0x24000>,
+			      <0x4 0x10000000 0x0 0x8000>,
+			      <0x4 0x10020000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x4 0x13044000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x4 0x13050000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			reg-names = "usb2phy", "pipehandler", "core", "axi2af", "lioa",
+				    "fabric", "common-config";
+			#phy-cells = <1>;
+			#reset-cells = <0>;
+			orientation-switch;
+			mode-switch;
+			power-domains = <&ps_atc2_usb>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * The ATC's display crossbar. Boards enable it with the external
+		 * display coprocessor whose fixed output uses it.
+		 */
+		atc2_dpxbar: mux@41304c000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-display-crossbar";
+			reg = <0x4 0x1304c000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			#mux-control-cells = <1>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_atc2_usb>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		atcphy3: phy@41aa90000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-atcphy";
 			reg = <0x4 0x1aa90000 0x0 0x4000>,
